{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 77.90.185.6 attempted a Path Traversal attack using URL-encoded sequences and double dots to break out of the intended web root directory. Specifically, they targeted sensitive system files like `/etc/passwd` and `/proc/self/environ`. The HTTP status codes (400 and 403) indicate that the web server or application firewall successfully blocked the unauthorized access attempts.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement strict input validation and normalization on all file path parameters to reject traversal sequences like '../' or encoded variations.",
    "Utilize built-in platform APIs or secure framework functions (e.g., java.nio.file or basename) that prevent directory traversal by design instead of manual string manipulation.",
    "Block or rate-limit the source IP address (77.90.185.6) at the Web Application Firewall (WAF) or edge router to prevent automated scanning."
  ]
}
